<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="8ed9e8a">Periodic status reporting should not replace, or otherwise substitute, providing full transparency. Information about
current progress, status or impediments should be readily available at all times to anyone interested. Transparency may be
provided either through the use of software tools or visual aids displayed in the team&apos;s working area, such as Burndown
Charts.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="29074861"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="514a8fb"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="dca895cc">&lt;p&gt;
    Report status to appropriate stakeholders and sponsors as agreed upon at the outset of the project. This report
    may&amp;nbsp;encompass any of the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Summary of project progress to date
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Projected results based on progress made thus far
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Current impediments such as identified risks or issues, as applicable
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work completed during most recent sprint
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work planned for next sprint
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Summary of any approved changes to current work/scope
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The level of detail provided in the report, regardless of the topic, should be adjusted to fit the targeted audience.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
